.TH QREDSHIFT 1 "2026" "qredshift" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qredshift \- Stateless C99 CLI for display color temperature, brightness, and gamma control on Linux. Native X11 and Wayland. Per-monitor targeting.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qredshift
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-i ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR kelvin ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR brightness ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR gamma ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR target ]\ .\|.\|.
.RB [ \-xlib ]
.RB [ \-interp ]
.RB [ \-wd ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qredshift
is a high-performance, stateless command-line utility for
adjusting screen color temperature, brightness, and gamma on
Linux. It is a modern replacement for
.BR redshift (1),
.BR sct (1),
and
.BR gammastep (1).
.PP
On X11,
.B qredshift
applies the requested gamma ramp immediately and exits; it keeps no
daemon and no configuration state, instead reconstructing its current
settings directly from the live hardware gamma ramps when needed. On
Wayland, where gamma control is tied to the compositor connection, it
runs a lightweight background daemon communicating over a FIFO pipe so
that later invocations apply instantly.
.PP
.B qredshift
supports independent per-display targeting via the
.B \-d
flag, and compiles to a ~40KB binary.
.PP
.B Key features:
native multi-monitor support, reverse gamma reconstruction without stored state, Wayland daemon mode with FIFO-based IPC, and a shared library plugin design that avoids pulling libwayland-client as a dependency on X11 systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage help.
.TP
.B \-v
Show program version.
.TP
.B \-i
Show information about connected displays, including their current
estimated temperature, brightness, and gamma.
.TP
.BI \-t \ kelvin
Set temperature in Kelvin, from 1000 to 25000. Defaults to 6500 (no color
shift). Calling
.B qredshift \-t
with no value resets to the default.
.TP
.BI \-b \ brightness
Set brightness, from 0.1 to 1.0. Defaults to 1.0.
.TP
.BI \-g \ gamma
Set gamma, from 0.1 to 5.0. Defaults to 1.0.
.TP
.BI \-d \ target
Target a specific display by index or RandR output name, optionally
overriding temperature, brightness, or gamma for that display only. May be
repeated to target multiple displays in a single call. Any parameter not
specified in a
.B \-d
block falls back to the global value set by
.BR \-t / \-b / \-g .
.RS
.PP
Syntax:
.I id
.RB [ :t= K ]
.RB [ :b= B ]
.RB [ :g= G ]
.PP man
Examples:
.RS
.PP
.B qredshift \-t 4500 \-d 1
.RS 0
target display 1 by index, using the global temperature
.RE
.PP
.B qredshift \-t 4500 \-d HDMI\-1
.RS 0
target display by RandR output name
.RE
.PP
.B qredshift \-t 6500 \-d 84:t=4500:b=0.8
.RS 0
display 84 overrides temperature and brightness; other displays get the global 6500K
.RE
.PP
.B qredshift \-d 84:t=6500:b=1.0 \-d 85:t=4500:b=0.8
.RS 0
two displays, fully independent settings
.RE
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B \-xlib
Use the Xlib backend instead of the default XCB backend.
.TP
.B \-interp
Use the legacy interpolation method for Kelvin-to-RGB conversion.
.TP
.B \-wd
Start the Wayland daemon without applying initial values. Only
available on Wayland sessions. The daemon listens on a FIFO pipe
for subsequent commands.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B qredshift \-i
.RS
.EX
Display Server: x11
Desktop Environment: X-Cinnamon
Mode: XCB RandR
84:C:DisplayPort-0:1920x1080 | T: 6500K | B: 1.00 | G: 1.00
85:C:DisplayPort-1:1920x1080 | T: 6500K | B: 1.00 | G: 1.00
.EE
.RE
.B qredshift \-d DisplayPort\-0 \-t 4000 \-b 0.85
.RS
Apply 4000K temperature and 85% brightness specifically to display connector DisplayPort-0.
.RE
.B qredshift \-d DisplayPort\-1:t=6500:b=1.0 \-d 84:t=4500:b=0.8
.RS
Two displays, fully independent settings.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non-zero on error (for example, no supported X11 or
Wayland display server detected, compositor missing required
protocols, or a display communication failure).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Used with
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
to detect a Wayland session and locate the compositor socket.
If found and accessible, the Wayland backend is selected.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Used to detect an X11 session. If
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is not present or its socket is unreachable, the X11 backend is
selected.
